{#-
  Flags passed to /usr/local/libexec/in.tftpd. Sourced by the netboot_tftpd
  rc.d wrapper. Runs in secure mode (chroot to content root), as user nobody,
  with IPv4+IPv6 listen on UDP/69.

  in.tftpd flags reference:
    -L     stay in foreground (we use this because daemon(8) supervises us)
    -s DIR chroot to DIR (secure mode)
    -u USR drop privileges to USR
    -p     permit only IPv4 (we omit this; we want dual-stack)
    -a A:P bind to specific address:port (we omit; bind to all, gate via firewall)

  This template must render even when the plugin is installed but not yet
  configured (i.e., no <netboot> section in config.xml). Without the
  helpers.exists guard, Jinja2's StrictUndefined raises on OPNsense.netboot
  before the default filter can fire, which fails the post-install template
  reload with 'collections.OrderedDict object has no attribute netboot'. The
  rendered file is harmless in that pre-config state since the rc.d wrapper
  only starts the daemon when general.enabled = 1 anyway.
-#}
{%- if helpers.exists('OPNsense.netboot.general.content_root') -%}
{%-   set content_root = OPNsense.netboot.general.content_root -%}
{%- else -%}
{%-   set content_root = '/var/netboot' -%}
{%- endif -%}
-L -s {{ content_root }} -u nobody
